Confirmation run: the small-sample winners, re-tested on more data
==============================================================================
  311,201 training rows, 776 validation rows, 776 features
  (previous run used a smaller sample)

==============================================================================
A. Does the shuffled split still inflate the score?
==============================================================================
  chronological split  PR-AUC 0.8908
  shuffled split       PR-AUC 0.9237
  inflation from shuffling: +0.0329

  The shuffled split puts the same cards and merchants on both sides of the
  boundary, so the model can memorise identities instead of learning fraud.
  That is why every number in this project comes from the time-based split.

